{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>and she</b> — until now, for she would say that the Baals, to whom she burns incense, are the ones who did her good, in the manner of 'and since we ceased burning incense to the host of heaven' [Jeremiah 44:18]." "<b>made for Baal</b> — the goldsmiths made forms of gold and silver to adorn the Baal. And in Spain there was a sage who explained 'the Baal' as the master of the house that grows in the wisdom of the constellations, for thus they call houses for the constellations, and it is them they worship, for they are the host of heaven."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:50.569464250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}